  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Circuits have both an item variant and stored analysis state. A dirty or damaged circuit, a clean unanalysed board, an analysed board and an analysed stable board are not interchangeable just because they share a number."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "text": "Processing route",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Extraction / Precision",
          "Find dirty or damaged circuits from their configured inputs."
        ],
        [
          "Restoration",
          "Clean dirty circuits into matching boards."
        ],
        [
          "Reassembly",
          "Repair damaged circuits into matching boards."
        ],
        [
          "Processing",
          "Combines the cleaning and repair roles."
        ],
        [
          "Analysis",
          "Analyse clean boards; reveals stability and can award items/FE."
        ],
        [
          "Fabrication / Plugs / Multiplication",
          "Use the exact board variants and state required by the operation."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Start with a raw chip and read its actual item name: Dirty or Damaged."
        ],
        [
          "Select the cleaning/repair machine that handles that type."
        ],
        [
          "After processing, move the resulting clean board into the Analysing Chamber."
        ],
        [
          "Read the analysed/stable tooltip before placing the board in a Fabrication recipe or Calculator Plug."
        ],
        [
          "Do not reinsert an already analysed board expecting another analysis reward."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The analyser has data-driven rewards. Its board state is saved on the item. The guide shows public instructions and recipe state requirements; it does not alter the board, reroll its data, or grant rewards."
    },
